<title>SLOVAKIA: Creditanstalt sells Slovak fund stake.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt sells Slovak fund stake.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria-based Creditanstalt Investment Bank AG (CAIB) on Tuesday said it had sold most of its 30 percent stake in the Slovak Creditanstalt Investment Fund a.s. (CASIF) to J&amp;T Securities II a.s..</p>
<p>Martin Cabadaj, director of CAIB's subsidiary Creditanstalt Securities, did not elaborate on the transaction details, but said the stake represented about 25 percent of the fund's shares out of CAIB's entire holdings of &quot;up to 30 percent&quot;.</p>
</text>
